{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 — fix, RED->GREEN, and replication\n\n### The fix (55 insertions, 0 deletions, 4 files)\n\nNew stdlib-only helper `detached_child_cwd(tracker)` in `src/rebar/_proc.py` — already this\nrepo's documented single source of truth for logic shared between detached-child spawn sites,\nand a deliberate leaf with no `rebar.*` imports, which the helper preserves. It returns the\nCANONICAL store's repo root: `os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(tracker))`, walked up to the\nnearest existing ancestor, ultimately `/`, which cannot be removed. It is total — it never\nraises, because all three call sites detach under a never-raise posture.\n\nAll three detach sites now pass it as `cwd=`:\n\n- `llm/enrich_drain.py::_spawn_detached_drain` -> `cwd=detached_child_cwd(tracker)`\n- `_commands/compact_trigger.py::_spawn_detached_sweep` -> `cwd=detached_child_cwd(tracker)`\n- `_store/push.py::push_tickets_branch` (async branch) -> `cwd=detached_child_cwd(base_path)`\n\n`realpath` is the load-bearing part, not tidiness: a provisioned worktree's\n`.tickets-tracker` is a SYMLINK into the main checkout, so the UNRESOLVED parent would be the\nvery worktree we are escaping. Taking the PARENT and not the tracker itself matters too — a\nchild sitting inside `.tickets-tracker` resolves the repo root to the tracker and then hunts\nfor a tracker inside the tracker.\n\nNothing else changed: `_detach_kwargs`, the child command strings, the tracker path passed as\nargv, and `_config_sources.repo_root` are all untouched. No test was modified or weakened, and\nno new dependency was added (`os` was already imported).\n\n### RED -> GREEN, with a held-out oracle\n\n`tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py` (new, 7 tests) was written and proven RED *before* any\nfix existed, then moved OUT of the working tree so the implementing subagent never saw it — it\nwas given only the contract, never the assertions or the path.\n\nRED, each for the right reason:\n- the behavioural test (real `_spawn_detached_drain`, real `rmtree` of the spawning worktree,\n  a real child reporting what it resolved) -> `ERR FileNotFoundError`, the production\n  traceback reproduced;\n- the three per-site tests -> recorded `cwd` is `None` at all three detach sites;\n- the three helper tests -> `ImportError`, the helper did not exist.\n\nGREEN: 7/7 pass against the fix the subagent wrote blind.\n\n**Mutation checks — five defect-seeded mutants, all returned the suite to RED**, and restoring\nreturned it to GREEN:\n\n| seeded defect | result |\n|---|---|\n| drop `cwd=` from `enrich_drain` | 2 failed |\n| drop `cwd=` from `compact_trigger` | 1 failed |\n| drop `cwd=` from `push` | 1 failed |\n| `realpath` -> `abspath` (stop seeing through the symlink) | 5 failed |\n| return the tracker instead of its parent | 6 failed |\n\nRefactoring litmus: the tests assert what a real child process resolves via `os.getcwd()`, and\nthe `cwd` argument handed to the OS at a real process boundary — plus INVARIANCE across two\ndifferent calling directories rather than a literal. No private name, no source grep, so a\nrename or a private extraction cannot redden them.\n\n### Replication of the original report, on THIS store\n\nSame scenario as the four production tracebacks: spawn the drain child from a directory whose\n`.tickets-tracker` symlinks the canonical store, then `rmtree` that directory while the child\nis alive. Two arms, identical but for `cwd=`:\n\n```\n[before] spawn cwd=None                       -> child exit=1, drain log grew by 1648 bytes\n         FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] ... in _config_sources.py:94  return Path.cwd()\n[after]  spawn cwd='/Users/joeoakhart/rebar'  -> child exit=0, drain log grew by 0 bytes\n```\n\nThe original report no longer reproduces: the child survives the removal of the worktree that\nspawned it and completes its drain run cleanly.\n\n### An honest limit on AC \"the three wedged entries drain\"\n\nThey do not, and this fix cannot make them. Chasing that criterion surfaced a SECOND,\nindependent cause, now filed as `spongy-illjudged-terrier` (569c-931f-69a2-4c1d) and linked\n`discovered_from` this ticket: `enrich()` builds an unbounded prompt, and for the three\nlargest tickets in this store it exceeds the model's context window —\n\n```\nprompt is too long: 206826 tokens > 200000 maximum   (400 ValidationException)\n```\n\nconfirmed by calling `enrich()` directly on `e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2` (fails in 2.8 s). `drain()`\ntreats that as transient and leaves the claim to lease-expire, so the entry cycles\nclaimed -> expired -> pending forever. I watched two full cycles twenty minutes apart\n(`drainer-41817-1` at 16:02, `drainer-63784-1` at 16:17), neither reaching `done`.\n\nSo the premise that this fix alone would silence the gate warning on this store is wrong, and\nI would rather say so than tick the box. Both causes must land before `958e`'s \"the WARNING no\nlonger fires on an ordinary write\" is observable here. What IS demonstrated is the equivalent\nreproduction the AC allows for: a detached drain child spawned from a since-removed worktree\nnow claims and completes instead of dying.\n\n### Siblings swept\n\nConstruct axis: every detached spawn in `src/rebar` — three sites, all with the same omission,\nall fixed here. Parity axis: the other three `start_new_session=True` uses\n(`grounding/harness.py:176`, `jira/acli_subprocess.py:443`,\n`jira_family/wiki_render.py:384`) are NOT detached — the flag is only there so a timeout can\n`killpg` the group, and the parent blocks on `communicate()`. Correctly out of scope, and\n`cwd=` would change nothing for them."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787268015673477001,"uuid":"5d4c5a7e-f76c-4edc-8408-4e175b4c826e"}